   512	\emph{Derivation of Theorem~\ref{thm:soft}.} The exact current of the
   513	model is $j^-_{x,x+1}=\frac{J}{2}(S^-_{x+1}-S^-_x)P_{x,x+1}$. A two-magnon
   514	eigenwave is free away from contact; writing the incoming coefficient as
   515	$1$ and the outgoing as $s(k_s,k_h)$, the single contact bond imposes
   516	\begin{equation}
   517	(2z_h-z_sz_h-1)\,s+(2z_s-z_sz_h-1)=0,\qquad z=\ec^{\ic k},
   518	\label{eq:contact}
   519	\end{equation}
   520	whose unique analytic solution near $k_s=0$ has $k_s$-coefficient $2\ic$,
   521	all hard dependence cancelling; the continuous logarithm gives
